# Iroh, Grand Lotus gives flashback to "instant and sorcery card[s] in your graveyard": the card is judged as it is in the
# graveyard, with only its normal characteristics (CR 715.4). Faithless Looting discards Lindblum, Industrial Regency (a
# land card whose Adventure is the instant Mage Siege) and Bonecrusher Giant (a creature card whose Adventure is the
# instant Stomp): in turn 3, with mana for either Adventure untapped, neither is offered flashback, while Faithless Looting
# is flashed back for {R} - the positive control. Then Octopus Form, an instant Lesson, is cast from the hand. "During
# your turn": in Bot2's turn 4, with {1} untapped, the Octopus Form has no flashback, and in Bot1's turn 5 it is cast for
# {1} and exiled.

